adsb_display — license
======================

**This plugin is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
(GPL-3.0-or-later)** — not the repository-root Apache-2.0 that covers the rest
of this repository.

It is the only GPL-licensed plugin here. The obligation comes from the aircraft
marker artwork described below, which is GPL-3.0 and cannot be relicensed. The
plugin's own source is distributed under the same terms so the combined work is
consistent.

You may obtain the full license text at <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0>.

Aircraft marker shapes
----------------------

`aircraft_shapes.h` is generated from tar1090's `markers.js`:

    tar1090 — https://github.com/wiedehopf/tar1090
    Copyright (C) Matthias Wirth and contributors
    GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0).

`scripts/convert_shapes.py` regenerates the header from that source: it fetches
`markers.js`, extracts the SVG path data, flattens the bezier curves and emits
the C++ polygon arrays. The generated file is committed for build reproducibility;
the script is the authority on how it was produced.

Individual shapes within that set carry their own upstream attribution:

  * the **C-130** icon originates from a FlightAware community thread, by
    **Peter Lowden**, marked in tar1090 as licensed under
    **CC BY 4.0** (<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>).
    Note: the original forum posting states no license; the CC BY 4.0
    designation is tar1090's.
  * the **A320 family**, **B737 family** and **e390** icons were contributed to
    tar1090 by **pimlie**. No separate license is stated for them upstream, so
    they fall under tar1090's GPL-3.0.

All other shapes are tar1090's own work under GPL-3.0.

Country flag images
-------------------

`embedded_flags.h` embeds 186 20x15 PNG country flags, generated from
`data/flags/` by `scripts/embed_flags.py`. `scripts/download_flags.py` fetches
them from:

    flagcdn.com / flagpedia.net — https://flagpedia.net/download

Flagpedia states the images are "completely free for commercial and
non-commercial use (public domain)", derived from Wikimedia Commons vector
files, with a backlink appreciated but not required. National flags are state
symbols and are generally not subject to copyright.

What this means when you redistribute
-------------------------------------

Distributing a built `adsb_display` binary carries the GPL-3.0 obligations for
the combined work: recipients are entitled to the corresponding source under the
same terms. That source is this directory, in this public repository.

The plugin loads at runtime against the Speculor engine (proprietary) across the
documented plugin C ABI, and links the Speculor Plugin SDK (proprietary). Those
are separate works with their own licenses; the GPL-3.0 grant on this plugin does
not extend to them, and their licenses do not restrict your rights to this
plugin's source.
